Memory Saver's timer puts a pinned tab to sleep like any other tab (issue #1069: with Memory Saver at Maximum, Top
Apps tiles and pinned rows, which are Chrome's pinned tabs, stayed loaded for hours at 200-450 MB each).
DiscardEligibilityPolicy keeps a pinned tab only from an urgent discard (memory pressure); a proactive or suggested
one takes it. MemorySaverModePolicy starts a pinned tab's timer however often it was revisited: the revisit cap
(more than 5 / 15 / 15 visits and a tab never sleeps) would exempt every tile in daily use for as long as it lives.
Every other protection is Chrome's: visible, a window's active tab, audible or recently audible, Picture in Picture,
capture, form input, PDFs, DevTools, kept-active sites, notifications, a title or icon changed in the background.

